king search finds, from each vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, extending through each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order to an unvisited vertex. Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/hamiltonianpath()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/hamiltonianPath()"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/edges-swift.associatedtype","type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Collection"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Edges"},"doc://Walks/documentation/Walks/Path":{"type":"topic","title":"Path","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Path","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A path: a walk that repeats no vertex, and so no edge.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Path","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/walks\/pat